1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,393
Strange Patent Applications.
奇怪的专利申请。

2
00:00:05,393 --> 00:01:32,853
I set about working in the current Patent Office after resigning from the court personnel. Competent and dynamic, I never feel passive while diving into the identifications of whether applications are valid and practical according to the new version of the criteria. With the expectation of distinguishing their own importance, some people leave the beaten track and file strange products with us now and then, for example, lantern that can be attached to your forehead, cubic walnuts, refrigerator made of straw and glue, perfume that nobody can bear to smell, and so on.
我开始在现在的专利局工作，是在从法院辞职之后。我能干而且精力充沛，从不觉得自己是在消极应付，而是深入开展审查，判断申请是否有效、是否实用，依据的是最新版本的标准。为了彰显自己的重要性，有些人不走寻常路，时不时向我们提交古怪的产品申请，比如能固定在额头上的灯笼，方形核桃、用稻草和胶水制成的冰箱，让人闻了无法忍受的香水，等等。

3
00:01:32,853 --> 00:02:17,613
Once, a man made a triangular helicopter out of stainless wires and string. He called us up and merrily claimed it was stable and convenient to use, and never out of order. I asked him to hang on, but this innocent man just rang off and set out to fly from his courtyard.
一次，一个人用不锈钢丝和绳子做了一架三角形直升机。他给我们打来电话，兴高采烈地声称它稳定、使用方便，而且从不出故障。我让他稍等，但这个天真的人直接挂断电话，开始从自家院子起飞。

4
00:02:17,613 --> 00:03:04,440
I dialed his number in the directory trying to ring him back, but never got through. By the mercy of God, an abrupt freezing rainfall made his powder wet. Luckily, the trouble was without any extension except that he crashed into a greengrocer’s making all the ripe fruits become messy jam.
我拨打通讯录里的号码，想给他回电话，却始终没接通。幸得上天眷顾，一场突如其来的冰冷降雨打湿了他的火药。幸运的是，事情没有进一步恶化，只是他撞进了一家蔬果店，把所有熟透的水果弄成了乱糟糟的果酱。

5
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:30,733
When people seized this crazy man with caution and sobered him by tapping his face, he complained about the bad weather instead of associating his failure with his unscientific design.
人们小心地抓住这个疯狂的人，轻拍他的脸让他清醒过来，他却抱怨起糟糕的天气，而没有把失败与自己不科学的设计联系起来。
